    *   **Logic:** The code uses `re.fullmatch(r'^[a-zA-Z0-9](?:[a-zA-Z0-9-]{0,61}[a-zA-Z0-9])?(?:\.[a-zA-Z0-9](?:[a-zA-Z0-9-]{0,61}[a-zA-Z0-9])?)*$', subdomain_prefix)` to validate the `subdomain_prefix`.
    *   **Explanation:**
        *   `^`: Matches the beginning of the string.
        *   `[a-zA-Z0-9]`: Ensures the first character of a label is alphanumeric.
        *   `(?:[a-zA-Z0-9-]{0,61}[a-zA-Z0-9])?`: This part handles the rest of a label.
            *   `[a-zA-Z0-9-]{0,61}`: Allows alphanumeric characters and hyphens, up to 61 characters.
            *   `[a-zA-Z0-9]`: Ensures the label does not end with a hyphen.
            *   `?`: Makes this entire middle part optional, allowing single-character labels.
        *   `(?:\.[a-zA-Z0-9](?:[a-zA-Z0-9-]{0,61}[a-zA-Z0-9])?)*`: This part handles subsequent labels separated by dots.
            *   `\.`: Matches a literal dot.
            *   `[a-zA-Z0-9](?:[a-zA-Z0-9-]{0,61}[a-zA-Z0-9])?`: This is the same pattern as the first label, ensuring each subsequent label is valid.
            *   `*`: Allows zero or more additional labels.
